---
import BaseHead from '../components/BaseHead.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import { SITE_TITLE } from '../consts';
import { ADS_REQUIRE_CONSENT } from '../config/site';

const updated = 'October 23, 2026';
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
	<head>
		<BaseHead
			title={`Privacy Policy — ${SITE_TITLE}`}
			description="What information the YTCPM website collects when you buy a license or contact us, why, where it is stored, and your choices."
		/>
		<style>
			main {
				padding: 0;
			}
			.band {
				background: var(--surface);
				border-bottom: 1px solid rgb(var(--gray-light));
				padding: 2.8em 0 2.4em;
			}
			.band h1 {
				font-size: clamp(2em, 4.6vw, 2.9em);
			}
			.band p {
				color: rgb(var(--gray-dark));
			}
			.body {
				padding: 2.6em 0 0.5em;
			}
			.inner {
				max-width: none;
			}
			.inner h2 {
				font-size: 1.35em;
				margin: 1.5em 0 0.5em;
			}
			.inner h2:first-child {
				margin-top: 0;
			}
			.inner p,
			.inner li {
				line-height: 1.7;
				color: rgb(var(--gray-dark));
			}
			.inner ul {
				margin: 0.4em 0 1em;
			}
		</style>
	</head>
	<body>
		<Header />
		<main>
			<section class="band bleed">
				<div class="wrap">
					<h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
					<p>Last updated: {updated}</p>
				</div>
			</section>
			<section class="body bleed">
				<div class="wrap">
					<div class="inner">
						<h2>Who we are</h2>
						<p>
							This policy covers the YTCPM website (ytcpm.cyou), which sells and
							supports the YTCPM Bot software. Questions about this policy or your
							information: use the <a href="/contact">contact page</a>.
						</p>

						<h2>What we collect</h2>
						<ul>
							<li>
								<strong>Order information.</strong> When you buy a license you give us
								your name, email address, an optional contact handle, the package you
								chose, the transaction hash of your payment (optional) and a screenshot
								of the payment as proof.
							</li>
							<li>
								<strong>Contact messages.</strong> When you write to us through the
								contact form: your name, email address, topic and message.
							</li>
							<li>
								<strong>Technical information.</strong> Our hosting provider keeps
								standard server logs (such as IP address and browser type) to run and
								secure the site. Signing in sets a session cookie that keeps you
								signed in. Analytics cookies are only set with your consent — see
								“Cookies and analytics” below.
							</li>
						</ul>

						<h2>Why we use it</h2>
						<p>
							To verify payments and activate licenses, to keep a record of your
							license, to answer your messages and provide support, and to keep the
							site working and secure. We do not use your information for advertising,
							and we never sell it.
						</p>

						<h2>Cookies and analytics</h2>
						<p>
							This site uses Google Analytics to understand how visitors use the
							site — but only if you allow it. When you first visit, a banner asks
							for your choice:
						</p>
						<ul>
							<li>
								<strong>Accept</strong> — Google Analytics loads and sets its
								cookies, which measure visits and page views.
							</li>
							<li>
								<strong>Decline</strong> — no analytics cookies are set, and the
								site works exactly the same.
							</li>
						</ul>
						<p>
							Your choice is remembered in your own browser (in local storage),
							never on our servers. You can change your mind at any time by
							clearing this site's data in your browser settings — the banner
							will ask again on your next visit. The cookies used for signing in
							are strictly necessary and are not used for analytics or
							advertising.
						</p>

						<h2>Advertising</h2>
						<p>
							This site uses Google AdSense to show ads on its public pages.
							{ADS_REQUIRE_CONSENT && (
								<>Ads load only if you accept cookies in the consent banner; if you decline, the ads script never runs. </>
							)}
							Third-party vendors, including Google, use cookies to serve ads
							based on your prior visits to this website or other websites.
							Google's use of advertising cookies enables it and its partners
							to serve ads to you based on your visits to this site and/or
							other sites on the Internet.
						</p>
						<p>
							You can opt out of personalized advertising at any time in
							Google's <a href="https://www.google.com/settings/ads" rel="noopener" target="_blank">Ads Settings</a>,
							or opt out of many third-party vendors' use of cookies for
							personalized advertising at
							<a href="https://www.aboutads.info/choices/" rel="noopener" target="_blank">aboutads.info/choices</a>.
							Ads never appear on the sign-in, account, checkout or admin
							pages.
						</p>

						<h2>Crypto payments</h2>
						<p>
							Payments are made in cryptocurrency to the addresses shown at checkout.
							We never receive or store bank or card details. Cryptocurrency
							transactions are recorded on public blockchains by design — a
							transaction hash you share with us can be viewed by anyone on a public
							blockchain explorer.
						</p>

						<h2>Where it is stored, and who can see it</h2>
						<p>
							Order records and contact messages are stored in our database, and
							payment screenshots are stored in a private file repository. Access is
							limited to us. We share information only with the infrastructure
							providers needed to operate the site (hosting and database), or when
							the law requires it.
						</p>

						<h2>How long we keep it</h2>
						<p>
							Order and license records are kept while your license is active and
							for a reasonable period afterwards for our records. Contact messages
							are kept until your question is handled. You can ask us to delete your
							information earlier — see below.
						</p>

						<h2>Your choices</h2>
						<p>
							You can ask us at any time what information we hold about you, and ask
							us to correct or delete it. Send the request through the
							<a href="/contact">contact page</a> using the same email address you
							ordered with, so we can find your records.
						</p>

						<h2>Security</h2>
						<p>
							Admin access to orders and messages is password-protected, and site
							secrets are stored as encrypted server variables. No system is
							perfectly secure, but we take reasonable steps to protect the
							information you give us.
						</p>

						<h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
						<p>
							If this policy changes, the new version will be posted on this page
							with an updated date at the top.
						</p>
					</div>
				</div>
			</section>
		</main>
		<Footer />
	</body>
</html>
